>1) How do I convert an alter from lawful or chaotic to neutral.. everytime I
> sacrafice it goes to chaotic.??

You're probably chaotic yourself.  If you sacrifice, there is a chance
that the altar will be converted to YOUR alignment. This chance is
bigger when you level is higher.

>2) How do I get rid of the aggrivate monsters intrinsic.? exclude gremlin's.

You can't, as far as I know.

>3) can a magic marker be used to 'write' in a blank spellbook for the higher
> level spells.. IE. genocide, polymorph, etc.?

You can "only" write scrolls/spellbooks you have already found
yourself. To be really honest, this isn't exactly true: any character
has a 1/15th chance of succesfully writing a previously unidentified
spellbook. I'm not sure if this is true for cscrolls as well, but I
think so. A wizard has a 1/3rd chance, btw.

>4) Is there anyway of rustproofing a 'named' sword if you didn't get it from
> a fountain or pick an already rustproofed one up?

This IS in the 7.00 spoilers: read a scroll of enchant weapon while
confused.

>5) I have tried many times to dip a longsword in the fountain to try and get
>excaliber. spoilers indicate that there is a chance IF excaliber isn't already
>in the game.. Q) How do you know if it Is or isn't in the game?

You cannot say it for sure, but if you've checked all ghost levels for
it, you can be pretty sure that it isn't in your game. Since Excalibur
will NEVER be randomly generated, bones levels are the only way
Excalibur can appear without you generating it yourself. If you are NOT
lawful, you cannot get it short of wishing for it, and even then, it
won't work for you, so don't bother.

>6) Is there anyway of bipassing lev 26 when level teleporting.?

Sounds like level 26 is your bottom level of the Dungeons of Doom.
Below, Gehennom (Hell) starts. This boundary cannot be crossed by means
of level teleporting.

